) (text "Pimoroni Pico Plus 2 (+ RM2 on SP/CE): same 40-pin header as Pico 2 W. I2C0 = GP4/GP5 (header pins 6/7), to the IMU\nQwiic-breakout header and to the 4-wire loom for the strain-gauge board. Crossed-out pins are intentionally unused." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 36 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "f7412098-d197-4b80-a4be-b6221f60d48d")) (text "NOTES\n1. ONE common GND (Pico, sensors, servo PSU). SBUS needs a shared ground reference.\n   RM2 WiFi breakout (off-board, cabled to the Pico Plus 2 SP/CE connector): uses GP32-GP36 only, no overlap with I2C (GP4/5) or any other signal.\n2. Strain gauges: SEPARATE board (kicad/gaugeboard), reached by a 4-wire I2C loom (GND, +5V, SDA, SCL; 0.1in headers, keyed plugs).\n   That board makes its own clean 3.3 V from +5V and holds both ADS122C04s, the gauge headers and the filtering.\n   ADS #2 needs its ADDR0 jumper bridged (expected address 0x41, unconfirmed; firmware scans at boot). I2C pull-ups come from the\n   ADS122C04 breakouts on the gauge board and from the IMU breakout.\n3. SBUS: GP20 (TX) and GP21 (RX) on one net (UART inverted in firmware). One 3x6 servo header (6 plugs of GND, V, SIG;\n   footprint HastaDAQ:PinHeader_3x06): V = VSERVO (8.4 V), SIG = SBUS (all six in parallel), GND.\n4. POWER: 12 V in, MAX 20 V (C1 is rated 25 V; silkscreen this at J8) (no fuse; the bench supply's current limit is the protection) -> +12V rail -> (a) Pololu D42V55F8 = VSERVO 8.4 V (servos), (b) SparkFun BabyBuck 5V = +5V (Orbis,\n   gauge-board loom, Schottky -> Pico VSYS). VSYS max is 5.5 V. USB (VBUS) is left for programming; with USB only, +5V is not live.\n   BabyBuck EN is left open (its own divider enables it). 5V bulk: module has 2x22uF; 100uF added near the Pico/ports.\n5. Triggers: TRIG_IN accepts 3.3-24 V (opto), TRIG_OUT is open collector with a jumper-selected pull-up. Pin order: see each symbol.\n   Main supply cable (2x4, pins 1-8 row-major): 1,8 VSUPPLY (12 V) | 2,7 VGND | 3 TRIG_IN | 6 TRIG_OUT | 4 SOFTSTOP+ | 5 SOFTSTOP-.\n   SOFTSTOP+ -> 1k -> GP16 (10k pull-up to 3V3, 5.1 V zener to GND), SOFTSTOP- = GND: loop closed = run, broken = stop.\n   The 2x4 connectors (this one and ENC1-4) are plain 0.1in headers for now; use keyed/shrouded plugs: a rotated plug would put 5V on a CS pin. Measured system current\n   was <= 1 A at 8.4 V, well inside ~3 A per 0.1in pin.\n6. Encoders: 4 x 2x4 headers (pins 1-8: GND, CS, SCK, MOSI, MISO, 3V3, 5V, GND) on one SPI1 bus; CS = GP13/GP9/GP8/GP7.\n   MT6835 uses 3V3 (3.3 V logic); RLS Orbis uses 5V with 3.3 V logic. Check MISO tri-states when CS is high.\n   The four ENC headers are a generic SPI port (SPI1: SCK GP10, MOSI GP11, MISO GP12, own CS each, 3V3 and 5V supply), so any 3.3 V\n   SPI device can be plugged in, not just encoders. Each device needs its own CS and an MISO that tri-states when CS is high." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 405 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "5cd2ad16-3bda-4d0b-8130-32cd5e80f949")) (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1"))) (embedded_fonts no))